{
  "_comment": [
    "Self-check spec for plugins/dev-loop/tools/mutate_verify.py — the harness pointed at its own source.",
    "Committed so the mutation numbers quoted in #60's PR are reproducible by a reviewer,",
    "rather than a property of a spec only the author ever saw. Run from the repo root:",
    "  python3 plugins/dev-loop/tools/mutate_verify.py run \\",
    "      --spec tools/mutation-specs/self-check.json \\",
    "      --test-cmd 'python3 -m unittest discover -s tests' \\",
    "      --root . --parent-root . --in-tree-authorized --timeout 600",
    "Expected: every entry killed, the single control survived, exit 0, tree byte-identical.",
    "--in-tree-authorized is REQUIRED here and is not a workaround: this self-check deliberately",
    "mutates the harness's own source in the repo root, so --root IS --parent-root and the",
    "attribution interlock refuses it (exit 5) without the flag. That is the interlock working.",
    "Anywhere other than this self-check, reach for a real isolated copy instead of the flag.",
    "A `find` that stops matching is a LOUD failure (exit 2), not a silent skip — so this file",
    "going stale is visible rather than quietly reducing coverage."
  ],
